# SESAME-style 3T-native EOS fixture for the [13c]/#11 unit test.
# Lines beginning with '#' are comments (skipped by the reader); numeric tokens
# are whitespace-delimited and consumed in order.
#
# Layout:
#   matid  ntables                      (material id, number of tables that follow)
#   then, for each table:
#     table_id  nr  nt                  (SESAME table id + grid dimensions)
#     density[nr]                       (g/cc, log-spaced ascending)
#     temperature[nt]                   (eV, log-spaced ascending)
#     <values>                          (EOS tables 301/303/304/305: P then E,
#                                        each nr*nt, density index fastest;
#                                        601 ionization: Zbar, nr*nt)
#
# 3T-native => an electron table (304) AND an ion table (305 or 303) are present.
# This fixture carries 304 (electron) + 305 (ion) + 601 (mean ionization). The
# reader derives the specific heat capacity cv = dE/dT from each species' energy.
#
# Synthetic laws, exact under (log-log) interpolation (T in eV, rho in g/cc):
#   e_ele = 1.5 rho^0.10 T   p_ele = 0.8 rho T   cv_ele = 1.5 rho^0.10
#   e_ion = 0.9 rho^0.05 T   p_ion = 0.5 rho T   cv_ion = 0.9 rho^0.05
#   zbar  = 3.0 + 0.5 log10(rho) + 0.25 log10(T)
#
# header: matid ntables
   3720   3
# --- SESAME table 304 (electron EOS) ---
